name: owner-actions
description: Record, present, update and retire the Ophiolite owner's actions and decisions - the single file the owner reads on the MacBook. Use when a lane or supervisor meets something only the owner may do (money, DNS, publication, credentials, deleting owner data, real people), when a decision is taken by default under the standing delegation, when the owner answers or completes an item, when asked "what do I need to do", or when tidying completed items.
---

# Owner actions

One file is the owner's to-do list and decision log; everything else (HANDOFF, PROGRAM, a
strategy) points at it by number. The owner reads it on the MacBook, in German time, and
does not read program documents to find actions. Rule since 29 September 2026: an action
that exists only in HANDOFF.md or PROGRAM.md does not exist.

## Where

| What | Path |
|---|---|
| Master (VPS) | `~/.local/share/ophiolite-owner-artifacts/ophiolite-owner-actions.md` |
| Completed items | `~/.local/share/ophiolite-owner-artifacts/ophiolite-owner-actions-completed.md` |
| Owner's copy (MacBook, user `sc`) | `~/Desktop/OphioliteLabs/` — the same two file names |
| Backups | `<file>.bak-<YYYY-MM-DD>` beside the master; one per day before the first structural edit |
| Side artifacts (scripts the owner runs, evidence folders) | the same directory, dated: `nlog-rights-2026-09-28/`, `configure-groningen-demo-2026-09-30.py` |
| The rules behind it | `PROGRAM.md` "Standing owner delegation" (what is decided by default, what is excluded); `HANDOFF.md` top entry "Standing owner delegation" |

The master is the VPS file. The Mac copy is overwritten from it after every edit
(`scripts/sync.sh`, which also compares checksums). Never edit the Mac copy.

## What is an owner action, and what is not

**Is** (the delegation's excluded list — never done by default; recorded, skipped, work
continues): deleting the owner's data (`~/ophiolite-staging`, the live database or its
volumes, backups); spending money or creating paid or external accounts; DNS, domain or
public-hosting changes; email or invitations to real people outside the test accounts;
making a repository, package or image public, or publishing third-party data the rights
register does not permit; creating, rotating or sharing credentials outside a lane's test
fixtures. Also: steps that need the owner's hands (a Mac or QGIS check, a phone), and
decisions the planner marks for the owner (`D<n>`).

**Is not**: anything a lane or the supervisor can do on the VPS inside the delegation —
restarting or recreating a test deployment (E15, lane containers), rerunning a hosted job,
choosing the recommended option of a strategy question, merging after green runs,
upgrading the private Workspace through the approved follow, refreshing a fixture. Those
are done and recorded in HANDOFF, plus one "Decided by default" line here when a
decision was involved. Writing "owner action" on something the delegation covers stalls
the program for a day (E15, 7 October).

**Publication is special.** "All approved" or "go with the recommended options" never
means publish: creating public repositories, pushing a candidate, changing visibility,
uploading to PyPI or making the image public wait for the owner's own sentence
"publish <release>" after the candidate report (#11). Record, do not infer.

## The file's shape (keep it)

```text
# Ophiolite owner actions
<header: when updated, where completed items are, the Mac aliases>
## Where the program is (<date>)          <- five lines, refreshed by the supervisor at each owner update
## Decided by default — review when convenient
- <d Mon HH:MM CEST> (<who>): <one line per default decision, newest first; what, why, where recorded>
## Now
### <n>. [ ] <Title> · <effort> · <when it is due or what it unblocks>
<what it is, in plain words; the exact Mac command or click path; what the owner answers;
 "Recommended:" when it is a decision; what happens after>
### <n>. [x] DONE <d Mon> — <evidence in one line>
## <family sections: Breadth program E52–E68, Real-world validation and scope, Later / deferred, Individual product follow-ups>
```

- **Numbers are permanent.** The next number is one more than the highest ever used (also
  in the completed file); never renumber, never reuse. Decisions keep their planner id in
  the title (`### 46. [ ] D23, D26–D28 …`).
- **One item, one decision or one hand action.** Several decisions of one family may share
  an item when they are answered together (#41 D15–D19).
- **Every item says**: effort (`~10 min`), timing (now / before X / optional / on hold),
  the recommended option for a decision, and the exact command or click path. Commands
  run in a Mac terminal; `oph` and `ophdoc` are aliases in the owner's `~/.zshrc`.
- **Plain words.** The owner reads German time and no engineering identifiers in the
  default text; hashes, run ids and paths go in a trailing "Technical" line.
- **No secrets.** Name a token (`vps-reserve`), never paste one. The Mac copy is a
  plain file on a Desktop.

## Who writes what

| Who | Writes |
|---|---|
| Execution worker (lane) | a new `### <n>. [ ]` item when it skips an excluded action; one "Decided by default" line per default decision, in the same step as the HANDOFF record; never marks DONE |
| Execution supervisor | rewrites items on the owner's answers ("rewrite #11 against release …"), marks `[x] DONE <date> — evidence` when the evidence exists, moves completed items, refreshes "Where the program is", presents the list |
| Planner | adds decision items (`D<n>`) with the recommendation and the lane that waits on them |
| Owner | answers in chat ("11 is fine", "yes", "go with recommended"); the supervisor writes the answer into the item and the record |

An agent that cannot tell whether something is excluded treats it as excluded, records it,
and continues with other work — it never asks (the worker's PreToolUse hook refuses
`AskUserQuestion`; off-switch `~/.claude/ophiolite-allow-questions`).

## How to edit (every time)

1. `python3 scripts/open.py` — see the open items and the next free number.
2. First structural edit of the day: `cp <file> <file>.bak-$(date +%F)`.
3. Edit with a unique anchor and an assertion (a Python `s.replace(old, new, 1)` after
   `assert s.count(old) == 1`), never by rewriting the file. Append "Decided by default"
   lines at the **top** of that list.
4. `scripts/sync.sh` — copies both files to the Mac and compares SHA-256; it prints
   `mac-ok` or the mismatch. Do not report the action as recorded before this prints `mac-ok`.
5. Point at the number from HANDOFF (`owner action 53`) and, for a lane, from the strategy's
   Validation Record.

## Marking done and tidying

- An item is DONE only with evidence the agent saw (a screenshot the owner sent, a record
  on the host, a run id, the owner's words quoted). Change `[ ]` to `[x] DONE <d Mon> —
  <evidence>`; keep the item in place until the next tidy so the owner sees it close.
- **Tidy** (supervisor, when "Now" has more than about five DONE items or the owner asks):
  move each DONE item verbatim into the completed file under `## Archived <date> — <theme>`,
  newest archive first; the decision text travels with it; the master keeps its number
  sequence. Sync both files. The completed file is the record that a decision was made;
  it does not claim implementation.
- A reversal by the owner ("undo D10") is a new "Decided by default" line naming the
  reversal and a hardening entry in HANDOFF, not a stop.

## Presenting the list to the owner

When asked "what do I need to do": the open items of "Now" in the order the program needs
them, each as one line — number, title, effort, what it unblocks — then "Later" in one
line. Mark what is waiting on the owner's own verification when they said they verify
first. Say which items the owner has already answered and are only waiting on the agent.
Give the Mac path once. Do not paste the file.

## Scripts

- `scripts/open.py` — prints open items (number, title, section) and the next free number;
  exits non-zero on a duplicate number.
- `scripts/sync.sh` — scp both files to the MacBook and compare checksums.
