name: devices
description: The machines, network, email accounts and object storage this owner operates - the ophiolite-epic-01 Hetzner VPS, the ophiolite-trial-01 trial and clean-machine server, a MacBook and iPhones on a Tailscale tailnet, and two Hetzner S3 buckets. Use when work involves picking a machine, reaching another device, using the golden-data or backup-proof buckets, reasoning about disk and CPU limits on the host, or choosing owner-controlled email accounts for authorized tests.
---

# Devices

Full inventory: `references/DEVICES.md`. Read it before acting on any specific
host, address or bucket — do not recall addresses from memory.

## Orientation

Almost all work happens on **ophiolite-epic-01**, the Hetzner VPS that runs the
epic fleet. If you are executing on Linux as user `epic` with `~/oph-agents`
present, you are on it. `ophiolite-dev` has priority over every other repo there.

## The four rules that actually bite

1. **Three servers are active: the controller, the trial server and the CI runner host.**
   `ophiolite-ci-01` (created 8 October 2026, Helsinki, project `ophiolite`) hosts
   self-hosted GitHub Actions runners for the private Integration repository only.
   `ophiolite-epic-01` does the work. `ophiolite-trial-01` (178.105.232.147,
   recreated 7 October 2026 in its own Hetzner project `ophiolite-trial`) is the
   clean machine for E79/E80 "Try it" proofs and the future trial and redirect
   host (owner actions 42, 52, 53). Sessions rebuild it themselves with the
   project-scoped `hcloud` token on the controller, so never keep state on it
   that must survive. Creating or deleting servers stays an owner action. The original `ophiolite-epic-worker-01` was deleted on
   2026-09-14; the pool worker and production VPS on 2026-09-26. Read the
   latest verification at the top of `references/DEVICES.md` before planning
   remote work; older sections retain historical details.

2. **Do not dispatch to a retired worker.** Historical fleet configuration may
   still name `remote-1`; a planner capability probe runs on the controller and
   does not prove a remote worker exists.

3. **Disk is the binding constraint on ophiolite-epic-01**, not CPU. ~200 GB of
   its 301 GB was used at the latest audit (including 55 GB owner seismic data).
   A full workspace build is ~37 GB. Never start a
   second heavy build while a lane is building — check `epic status` for a live
   runner first. Exhausting the disk kills the lane runner mid-ticket and loses
   its uncommitted work; this has happened three times.

4. **Never delete `~/ophiolite-staging`.** It is 55 GB of the owner's seismic
   data (SEGY volumes, wells, horizons, tops), not build output.

## Reaching other devices

The tailnet is `tail76622e.ts.net`: `ophiolite-epic-01`, `ophiolite-ci-01`, `macbook`, `iphone-15`,
`iphone-11`. `ophiolite-trial-01` is reached by its public address until it
joins the tailnet.

Who can log in where, with which key, plus the token, GitHub and live-Workspace
access: the table "Access and authentication" at the top of DEVICES.md. Short
form: Mac → `ssh -o BatchMode=yes ophiolite-epic`; controller → `ssh macbook`,
`ssh trial`; Hetzner API (trial project only) → `~/.local/bin/hcloud`; `gh` is
`tuna-soup` on both machines.

The home Samsung TV (Netflix stop) is not on the tailnet; it is reached through the MacBook. See the `tv-stop` skill and the Home LAN section of DEVICES.md.

## Domains and public names

Domains are at Spaceship (registrar and DNS): `ophiolite.dev` is live today;
`ophiolite.systems` is the product address being cut over to (E83, owner action 53; apex and
`www` → GitHub Pages, `*.try` → trial server);
`ophiolite.io` and `ophiolitelabs.com` are held. GitHub organisation `ophiolite-labs` and
PyPI `ophiolite` (account `stefcroo`) are reserved. See "Domains and DNS" and "Public names
and registries" in DEVICES.md before touching DNS or publishing anything.

## Object storage

Hetzner S3 at `https://nbg1.your-objectstorage.com`, region `nbg1` (send `nbg1`
or Hetzner rejects the request). `ophiolite-golden-data` is the golden test
corpus; `ophiolite-backup-proof` holds backup-harness output, and the backup
harness must never touch the golden bucket. Credentials come from the
environment — never commit or echo them.

## Email accounts for testing

Read [references/EMAIL.md](references/EMAIL.md) before choosing a sender, recipient,
SMTP credential or Gmail route for authorized email testing. It records qualified
Proton submission, Gmail receipt access, other owner addresses and private
credential locations; it contains no secrets.

## Keeping this accurate

Re-verify before relying on a detail; hosts drift. Useful checks:
`hostname`, `df -h /`, `tailscale status`, and the Hetzner audit in
`references/DEVICES.md`. When something has changed, update that file rather
than working around it.

